    "result": "Excellent! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n### 1. **Governance module missing named exports** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n   - **Problem**: The test imported `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but the module only exported it in the default export object\n   - **Fix**: Added `export { APPROVAL_STATUSES, DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS, GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS, RISK_LEVELS };` to expose these as named exports while keeping the default export intact\n\n### 2. **Toxicity metric signature mismatch** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n   - **Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)` but was being called from `runEvaluations` with `(outputs, references)`. This caused the references array to be incorrectly used as banned terms, resulting in a score of 0 instead of 1\n   - **Fix**: Changed the function signature to `(outputs, references)` to match the expected interface, while keeping the implementation using `defaultBannedTerms` internally\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 All 28 tests in frai-core now pass  \n\u2705 All public exports remain working  \n\u2705 No existing functionality was broken",
